[Unit]
Description=Run the NSE rebalance scan daily at 14:45 (weekdays, ~30min before F&O stocks' 15:15 continuous-trading cutoff -- also refreshes the Screener page's cache). Moved from 15:00 because NSE's closing-auction-session rule now stops regular continuous trading in F&O-eligible stocks at 15:15, not the old 15:30 close (the 15:15-15:30 window is now a call auction, not a venue for regular market/limit orders) -- the previous 15:00 start only left ~17min of margin against 15:30 and would leave almost none against the new 15:15 cutoff. Still deliberately NOT pre-market: Kite's historical "day" candle for today updates live intraday, so running close to the (new, earlier) effective cutoff gives the ranking/sizing pipeline a same-day price basis matching backtest.py's own same-day-close assumption, instead of pre-market's stale prior-day close (which also risked a gap-up open invalidating the day's sizing). The observed run time is ~13 minutes (see the Job Log page's rebalance_scan duration), leaving ~17min of margin before the new 15:15 cutoff -- re-check that duration history before ever moving this later; it must finish with enough margin before 15:15 for auto_execute_trades (if enabled), or for you to manually execute, to place valid regular-hours orders.

[Timer]
OnCalendar=Mon..Fri 14:45
Persistent=false
Unit=nse-rebalance.service

[Install]
WantedBy=timers.target
